hierarchy":{"lvl1":"INFO-H515 - Big Data Scalable Analytics","lvl3":"Start Spark session","lvl2":"RDD example"},"content":"A Spark session is created by using the pyspark.sql.SparkSession object. See \n\nhere for the API documentation on the SparkSession Object.\n\n#This is needed to start a Spark session from the notebook\nos.environ['PYSPARK_SUBMIT_ARGS'] =\"--conf spark.driver.memory=2g  pyspark-shell\"\n\nfrom pyspark.sql import SparkSession\n\n\n\n#Uncomment below to recreate a Spark session with other parameters\n#spark.stop()\nspark = SparkSession \\\n    .builder \\\n    .master(\"local[4]\") \\\n    .appName(\"demoRDD\") \\\n    .getOrCreate()\n    \n#When dealing with RDDs, we work the sparkContext object. See https://spark.apache.org/docs/latest/api/python/pyspark.html#pyspark.SparkContext\nsc=spark.sparkContext\n\n\n\n","type":"content","url":"/demordd-local#start-spark-session","position":9},{"hierarchy":{"lvl1":"INFO-H515 - Big Data Scalable Analytics","lvl3":"Start dummy Spark jobs","lvl2":"RDD example"},"type":"lvl3","url":"/demordd-local#start-dummy-spark-jobs","position":10},{"hierarchy":{"lvl1":"INFO-H515 - Big Data Scalable Analytics","lvl3":"Start dummy Spark jobs","lvl2":"RDD example"},"content":"\n\n# Wait function\ndef wait2s(x):\n    time.sleep(2)\n    return x\n\n\n\nn_partitions=8\n\ndata=range(0,n_partitions)\ndatardd=sc.parallelize(data,n_partitions)\n\ndatardd.map(wait2s).collect()\n\n\n\n\n\n","type":"content","url":"/demordd-local#start-dummy-spark-jobs","position":11},{"hierarchy":{"lvl1":"INFO-H515 - Big Data Scalable Analytics","lvl3":"Open Spark UI and check parallelisation","lvl2":"RDD example"},"type":"lvl3","url":"/demordd-local#open-spark-ui-and-check-parallelisation","position":12},{"hierarchy":{"lvl1":"INFO-H515 - Big Data Scalable Analytics","lvl3":"Open Spark UI and check parallelisation","lvl2":"RDD example"},"content":"Open Spark UI at 127.0.0.1:4040 (192.168.99.100:4040 if you are running a Docker with Docker Toolbox)",